# Environment files are split by Supabase target. Copy ONE of these (never commit the copy):
#   .env.local.example  -> .env.local  (Supabase Docker stack on this machine)
#   .env.cloud.example  -> .env.cloud  (supabase.com project)
# Select at run time:  $env:ENV_FILE=".env.local"; docker compose up -d --build   (default: .env)
# Empty SUPABASE_URL/SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = browser-only local mode.
# Details: docs/08-ops/SUPABASE_ENVIRONMENTS.md
